# Machine overlay map — copy to machine-map.conf and list your own machines.
#
# Each line: <host-glob>[:<user-glob>] <overlay>
#   host-glob  shell glob matched against the hostname (DESKTOP-*, my-laptop, srv-??)
#   user-glob  optional; the line only matches when the login user also matches
#   overlay    a directory under setup/config/machines/ holding that machine's overrides
# First matching line wins. '#' starts a comment. No match → no overlay (base config only).
#
# One-shell override without editing this file:  FLEET_MACHINE=<overlay> bash sync.sh deploy
# Logic too complex for globs? Define local_machine_map <host> <user> in sync.local.sh;
# it is consulted when no line here matches.

my-desktop-*        wsl
my-laptop:me        fedora-home
my-laptop:work-me   office
my-vps              vps
